%% Sequence 02e — Task submission to review handoff
%% Evidence status: Implemented.
%% Parent use case: UC 02b “Submit completion package and enter review”.
%% Design-class trace: cls_02l_task_submission_runtime_design defines the concrete controller, command, transaction, governance, and fan-out responsibilities summarised by this interaction.
%% Scenario: an assignee submits one completion package with evidence.
%% Scope: one successful transaction, its durable outputs, and its review handoff. The abbreviated lifeline labels keep the sequence at one interaction viewpoint; the preceding design-class diagram names the concrete collaborators.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Assignee
    participant C as «boundary» Submission API
    participant K as «control» Submission command
    participant DB as «store» PostgreSQL transaction
    participant R as «outbound» Review + delivery coordinator

    A->>C: POST submission package
    C->>K: execute(package)
    activate K
    K->>DB: Lock task, assignment, and submission
    DB-->>K: Current records
    K->>K: Validate actor, package, and policy
    K->>DB: Persist submission, evidence, and snapshot
    K->>R: Create review handoff and stage audit/fan-out
    R->>DB: Persist handoff and durable delivery work
    DB-->>K: Commit authoritative records
    K-->>C: submissionId and reviewSessionId
    deactivate K
    C-->>A: 201 submission accepted
